    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0502" n="1236" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1236"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 461.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for your information,
                    copy of a letter of the 7th instant from the foreign secretary of the American
                    Board of Commissioners for Foreign Missions, expressing the gratification of the
                    Board at the favorable outcome of your efforts in behalf of Marsovan
                    College.</p>
                <pb facs="0503" n="1237" xml:id="pg1237"/>
                <p>Mr. Smith, expresses the hope that the Sultan will go further and extend the same
                    protection to the Protestant church in Stamboul, which has long awaited such
                    action on his part.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d492-a1.xml" xpointer="d492-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
